        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3cb1e65f-04ef-5365-b4c9-4cdc45ab9311",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Royal Albert Hall, South Kensington, London, Wolverhampton Civic Hall, Paradiso, Amsterdam, La Luna, Brussels\n- Products: Live Wood, The Best of Nanci Griffith\n- Events: concerts, Proms concerts\n- Topics: live recordings, concert dates\n\nFacts:\n- The Royal Albert Hall is a concert hall on the northern edge of South Kensington, London.\n- The Royal Albert Hall has hosted the Proms concerts annually each summer since 1941.\n- \"The Road To Aberdeen,\" a previously unreleased song on The Best of Nanci Griffith, was recorded live at the Royal Albert Hall in London in June 1993.\n- Songs for Live Wood were chosen from concerts including the Royal Albert Hall, London, on 22 November 1993, although that date was incorrectly listed as December.\n- Songs for Live Wood were also chosen from concerts at Wolverhampton Civic Hall on 9 March 1994, the Paradiso in Amsterdam on 16 April 1994, and La Luna in Brussels on 17 April 1994.",
